course: dictionary
lesson: 15621
title: Teased: fun or hurtful?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Teased» can mean laughed at someone or made jokes about them. To work out which kind of teasing it is, look at the words around it. Are both people laughing, or is one person upset?
explain: «Mia teased her brother about his red wellies, and they both giggled.» Both of them are laughing, so this is friendly and playful. Now compare: «The boys teased Sam about his glasses every day, and he went quiet.» Sam is hurt, and it keeps happening, so this teasing is unkind.
explain: «Teased» has other meanings too. «The dog teased the cat by holding its toy just out of reach» means it annoyed the cat on purpose. «She teased out the answer» means she slowly worked it out. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: If someone teases you in a way that hurts you, tell a trusted adult. Nobody should be made to feel small or left out.
fact: «Teased» is the past form of the verb «tease».
fact: «Teased» can mean laughed at someone, in a friendly way or in an unkind way that hurts.
fact: «Teased» can mean annoyed an animal on purpose, and an animal that is teased may bite or scratch.
fact: «Teased out» means slowly found or worked out, as in «she teased out the answer».
fact: Teasing becomes bullying when it hurts someone, keeps happening, or is about looks, family, culture or disability.
exercise: «Mia teased her brother about his wellies, and they both giggled.» What does teased mean here? | Annoyed an animal on purpose | Slowly worked out | *Laughed at each other in a friendly, playful way | Gently combed
exercise: «The dog teased the cat by holding its toy just out of reach.» What does teased mean? | Hugged tightly | Told a joke to | *Annoyed on purpose | Gently combed
exercise: «The boys teased Sam about his glasses every day, and he went quiet.» Why is this teasing not fun? | It is about the weather | Nobody noticed it | *Sam is hurt, and it keeps happening | Both boys are laughing and Sam is laughing too
test: «She teased out the answer after a long think.» What does teased out mean? | Lost the answer | Shouted loudly | *Slowly found or worked out | Forgot it completely
test: Ben says, «Only teasing!» after he has hurt Jo's feelings again and again. What should Jo do? | *Tell a trusted adult | Tease him back even harder | Keep quiet and hope it stops | Hide his bag
exam: Which sentence uses teased to mean laughed at someone in a friendly way? | *«Mum and I teased each other and laughed over the silly joke.» | «The cat teased the fish.» | «She teased out the tangles in her hair.» | «The boys teased Sam until he cried.»
